```js
export async function drain(source, handle) {
  let handled = 0;
  for (;;) {
    const item = await source.next();
    if (item === null) return handled;
    await handle(item);
    handled++;
  }
}
```

- Pulls via `source.next()`, stops on `null` (strict, so `0`/`false` items still count), awaits `handle` before pulling again, returns the count.
- JSDoc with `@returns` sits directly above the export (rule 9).
